'Warp-grinder', 'Weapon Team'),\000d\000a\000d\000a-- Plague Monks\000d\000a(50, 10, 3, 'Champion', 'Champion', 'SingleBuy'),\000d\000a(51, 5, 3, 'Musician', 'Musician', 'SingleBuy'),\000d\000a(52, 10, 3, 'Standard Bearer', 'Standard Bearer', 'SingleBuy'),\000d\000a\000d\000a-- Warlock Engineer\000d\000a(53, 0, 22, 'Grants One spell', 'Level 1 Wizard', 'Magic'),\000d\000a(54, 35, 22, 'Grants One more spell', 'Level 2 Wizard', 'Magic'),\000d\000a(55, 4, 22, 'Grants +2 Strength in first turn of combat', 'Flail', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(56, 2, 22, 'Grants One more attack', 'Additional hand Weapon', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(57, 10, 22, 'Add 10 points to attack', 'Warplock Pistol', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(58, 0, 22, 'Add armor save', 'Warp Armor', 'Armor'),\000d\000a(59, 15, 22, 'Add 15 points for a shield', 'Shield', 'Armor'),\000d\000a(60, 20, 22, 'Add 20 points for a Warplock Pistol', 'Warplock Pistol', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(61, 0, 22, 'Flee 1"" more', 'Scurry Away', 'Race special rule'),\000d\000a(62, 0, 2, 'Grants More Ld for each rank (max 10Ld)', 'Strength in numbers', 'Race special rule'),\000d\000a\000d\000a-- GreySeer\000d\000aINSERT INTO UPGRADE (ID, POINTS_COST, UNIT_ID, DESCRIPTION, NAME, UPGRADE_TYPE) VALUES\000d\000a(63, 200, 10, 'Screaming Bell', 'Screaming Bell', 'Mount'),\000d\000a(64, 4, 10, 'Musician', 'Musician', 'SingleBuy'),\000d\000a(65, 8, 10, 'Standard Bearer', 'Standard Bearer', 'SingleBuy'),\000d\000a(66, 0.5, 10, 'Spears', 'Spears', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(67, 0.5, 10, 'Shields', 'Shields', 'Weapon'),\000d\000a(68, 65, 10, 'Special Weapon Team', 'Poisoned Wind Mortar', 'Weapon Team'),\000d\000a(69, 70, 10, 'Special Weapon Team', 'Warp Fire Thrower', 'Weapon Team'),\000d\000a\000d\000a(70, 15, 10, 'A warpmusket is a rifle built along the same lines as\000d\000a             the warplock jezzail, although not as long of barrel.\000d\000a             A warpmusket isamove or fire weapon that has a\000d\000a             range of 24"" and is Strength 5. A warpmusket is\000d\000a             Armour Piercing, uses Unstable Ammunition (see\000d\000a             page 65), and is a Warpstone Weapon.', 'Warpmusket', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(71, 15, 10, 'The fine powders and unctuous lotions purchased\000d\000a             from Clan Eshin can turn a scratch into a deathblow.\000d\000a             All close combat attacks made by the model count as\000d\000a             Poisoned Attacks. This will affect a tail weapon, but\000d\000a             not any magic weapons or a Rat Hound Bodyguard.', 'Poisoned Attacks', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(72, 8, 10, 'This could be a mechanical Clan Skryre attachment\000d\000a             or an evolved mutation, the results are the same\000d\000a             another appendage wielding a weapon.\000d\000a             A model with this additional blade, spike or mace can\000d\000a             make an additional S3 Attack at the user's WS and\000d\000a             Initiative. It can be used in addition to other attacks\000d\000a             including an additional hand weapon or even a magic\000d\000a             weapon, although it gains no magical properties.', 'Tail Weapon', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(73, 8, 10, 'The puny pistols of other races pale in comparison to\000d\000a            the Warlock Engineer's constructions.\000d\000a            A warplock pistol follows the rules for pistols except\000d\000a            that it has a range of 10"". A warplock pistol is Armour\000d\000a            Piercing, uses Unstable Ammunition (see page 65),\000d\000a            and is a Warpstone Weapon.', 'Warplock Pistol', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(74, 5, 10, 'There is a certain hound-like loyalty to these\000d\000a            modified rats, although their verminous instincts\000d\000a            means they might still attack their master if be\000d\000a            appears vulnerable.\000d\000a            A model with a Rat Hound upgrade can make an\000d\000a            additional WS3. S3 attack. This attack is made at the\000d\000a            owner's Initiative, however, on a To Hit roll of 1 the rat\000d\000a            hound will instead inflict an automatic hit on its owner.', 'Rat Hound Bodyguard', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a\000d\000a\000d\000a(75, 0, 10, 'These pieces of refined warpstone are consumed by\000d\000a              power-bungry Grey Seers or Warlock Engineers to aid\000d\000a              their spellcasting. This is dangerous, but the quick\000d\000a              road to power is an irresistible pull for any Skaven.\000d\000a              Multiple Grey Seers and Warlock Engineers may\000d\000a              purchase as many Warpstone Tokens as are allowed\000d\000a              within the limit of points they are able to spend on\000d\000a              magic items. Warpstone Tokens do not count against\000d\000a              the total Arcane itemssaa model is allowed to bea\000d\000a              A Grey Seer or Clan Skryre Warlock may choose to eat\000d\000a              some warpstone to boost his powers. Before casting a\000d\000a              spell announce which model is eating Warpstone Tokens.\000d\000a              For each token consumed, a Wizard can add a single dice\000d\000a              to his casting effort. These dice are added to the normal\000d\000a              power dice, although this does allow users to roll more\000d\000a              dice than is normally allowed by their level. A spell may\000d\000a              be cast entirely with warpstone.\000d\000a              For any of the warpstone generated dice that rolls a\000d\000a              one the Wizard suffers a wound with no armour saves\000d\000a              allowed. The results of miscasts or irresistible forc\000d\000a              apply as normal. When using both normal power dice\000d\000a              and Warpstone Token generated dice it is a good idea\000d\000a              to roll separately or use dice ofa different colour\000d\000a              (green-tinged ones work best[*]!).', 'D3 Warpstone tokens', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(76, 0, 10, 'Free hand weapons to fight', 'Hand Weapon', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(77, 0, 10, 'Grants 4 spells from Ruin or Plague Spells', 'Lvl 4 Wizzard', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(78, 0, 10, ' Skaven characters with this rule\000d\000a             can refuse a challenge with no loss of honour. Other\000d\000a             races see such acts as cowardly, but Skaven view a\000d\000a             commander scampering to safety and dooming those\000d\000a             underneath him as a leader's natural right.\000d\000a             If a Skaven character refuses a challenge, the model is\000d\000a             placed in the back rank as normal, however, the unit\000d\000a             may still use the Skaven character's Ld or Battle\000d\000a             Standard ability even after the character has been\000d\000a             moved to the back.', 'Verminous Valour', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(79, 0, 10, ' The Skaven embody the adage 'he who\000d\000a             runs away lives to fight another day!' All models in the\000d\000a             Skaven army add add +1 to the total rolled to determine\000d\000a             the distance they flee.', 'Scurry Away', 'Race special rule'),\000d\000a(80, 0, 10, 'Skaven are not brave by nature,\000d\000a             but do take courage from being in large packs of their\000d\000a             own kind. All units in the Skaven army add their\000d\000a             current rank bonus to their Leadership value for any\000d\000a             Leadership-based test.\000d\000a             To calculate the Leadership of a unit with the Strength\000d\000a             in Numbers rule, first determine the unit's Leadership\000d\000a             as normal and then add the rank bonus of the unit to\000d\000a             this value, up to a maximum Leadership of 10.\000d\000a             For example, a 15 model-strong unit of Clanrats (Ld 5)\000d\000a             deployed in three ranks of five would receive a +2\000d\000a             rank bonus for a total Leadership of 7. If a Chieftain\000d\000a             (Ld 6) led the unit, the value would go up to a\000d\000a             Leadership of 8. If the unit was within a 12"" range\000d\000a             of a Warlord that was the Skaven General (Ld 7),\000d\000a             the unit would go up to Leadership 9.\000d\000a             Note that a Skaven General confers his basic Leadership\000d\000a             and then units modify it with their own rank bonus.\000d\000a             Any bonus from the ranks of the General's unit is not\000d\000a             passed on to units within 12"".\000d\000a             If for any reason a Skaven unit loses its rank bonus,\000d\000a             it also loses its Leadership bonus. For instance, fleeing\000d\000a             units do not have a rank bonus, so fleeing Skaven must\000d\000a             use their basic Leadership.', 'Strength in numbers', 'Race special rule');"
