   page 65), and is a Warpstone Weapon.', 'Warpmusket', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(71, 15, 10, 'The fine powders and unctuous lotions purchased\000d\000a             from Clan Eshin can turn a scratch into a deathblow.\000d\000a             All close combat attacks made by the model count as\000d\000a             Poisoned Attacks. This will affect a tail weapon, but\000d\000a             not any magic weapons or a Rat Hound Bodyguard.', 'Poisoned Attacks', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(72, 8, 10, 'This could be a mechanical Clan Skryre attachment\000d\000a             or an evolved mutation, the results are the same\000d\000a             another appendage wielding a weapon.\000d\000a             A model with this additional blade, spike or mace can\000d\000a             make an additional S3 Attack at the user's WS and\000d\000a             Initiative. It can be used in addition to other attacks\000d\000a             including an additional hand weapon or even a magic\000d\000a             weapon, although it gains no magical properties.', 'Tail Weapon', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(73, 8, 10, 'The puny pistols of other races pale in comparison to\000d\000a            the Warlock Engineer's constructions.\000d\000a            A warplock pistol follows the rules for pistols except\000d\000a            that it has a range of 10"". A warplock pistol is Armour\000d\000a            Piercing, uses Unstable Ammunition (see page 65),\000d\000a            and is a Warpstone Weapon.', 'Warplock Pistol', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a(74, 5, 10, 'There is a certain hound-like loyalty to these\000d\000a            modified rats, although their verminous instincts\000d\000a            means they might still attack their master if be\000d\000a            appears vulnerable.\000d\000a            A model with a Rat Hound upgrade can make an\000d\000a            additional WS3. S3 attack. This attack is made at the\000d\000a            owner's Initiative, however, on a To Hit roll of 1 the rat\000d\000a            hound will instead inflict an automatic hit on its owner.', 'Rat Hound Bodyguard', 'The Scavenge-Pile'),\000d\000a\000d\000a\000d\000a(75, 0, 10, 'A Grey Seer or Clan Skryre Warlock may consume warpstone to enhance magic. Before casting, declare tokens used. Each adds one dice to casting rolls, even beyond the normal limit. A spell may be cast entirely with warpstone. If a warpstone dice rolls a 1, the Wizard suffers a wound with no armour save. Miscasts and irresistible force apply as usual. When mixing normal and warpstone dice, roll separately or use different colours, green being traditional.', 'D3 Warpstone tokens', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a                (76, 0, 10, 'Free hand weapons to fight', 'Hand Weapon', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a                (77, 0, 10, 'Grants 4 spells from Ruin or Plague Spells', 'Lvl 4 Wizzard', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(78, 0, 10, 'Skaven characters may refuse a challenge without loss of honour. While other races see this as cowardice, Skaven regard fleeing to safety and sacrificing followers as a leader[*]’s right. When refusing, the model moves to the back rank as usual, but the unit may still benefit from the character’s Leadership or Battle Standard ability even after he has been placed in the rear.', 'Verminous Valour', 'Free upgrade'),\000d\000a(79, 0, 10, ' The Skaven embody the adage 'he who\000d\000a             runs away lives to fight another day!' All models in the\000d\000a             Skaven army add add +1 to the total rolled to determine\000d\000a             the distance they flee.', 'Scurry Away', 'Race special rule'),\000d\000a(80, 0, 10, 'Skaven are not brave, but gain courage from numbers. With Strength in Numbers, a unit adds its rank bonus to Leadership for tests, to a maximum of 10. For example, Clanrats with Ld 5 in three ranks get +2, for Ld 7. A Chieftain raises this to 8, a nearby Warlord (Ld 7) to 9. The General gives only his base Leadership, not his unit’s bonus. If a unit loses rank bonus, it also loses the Leadership bonus, such as when fleeing.', 'Strength in numbers', 'Race special rule');"
